  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "rivet": "solid rivets",
    "squeezer": "squeezer practice",
    "card": "Insert and set three original solid rivets on an instructional squeezer frame.",
    "wrong_stage": "Insert this numbered rivet only from its rack, then set it only while inserted. A set joint is permanent on this fixture.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free for the numbered practice control.",
    "howto_rivet": "Each fixed numbered control operates its matching numbered joint and original rack rivet. First insert that rivet through the two aligned open holes, then set its exposed rear tail into a wider, shorter shophead. The original front manufactured head stays unchanged. The two predrilled strips are prealigned and clamped; integral indexed dies/backing meet both head faces at the set pose. Other joints remain independent. Each fixture is supplied for three permanent practice joints: there is no reset, reload, extraction, loose stock or output to carry. This attached instructional depiction snaps between indexed poses. It does not simulate drilling, impacts, continuous squeezing/contact paths, precise material volume, forces, load-bearing strength, real fabrication or aircraft work. The hand touches a practice control; anatomical rivet-working contact is not guaranteed."
  },
